server: run a duplication of another process's semaphore in that process

ntdll recycles a private unnamed semaphore after the application closed it and stops when
the handle is duplicated by its own process. dup_handle for a semaphore of another,
initialized process, with in-process sync and without fsync, answers
STATUS_MORE_PROCESSING_REQUIRED; the caller's ntdll then runs the duplication in the source
process as APC_DUP_HANDLE, as it already does for DUPLICATE_CLOSE_SOURCE. Other object
types and duplications within the caller's own process keep the direct path.

See dlls_ntdll_unix_sync_c_semaphore_recycle.patch.

